  // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
  // The previous strategy returned the input unchanged, so it never produced any
  // solution text, never emitted the required << >> arithmetic delimiters, and
  // never exposed an extractable answer. To address those failures while still
  // preserving parser validity, this strategy actively decodes up to maxSteps
  // tokens from the current valid prefix.
  //
  // The core strategy is:
  // 1. Continue from currentPrefix, maintaining generated as the full output.
  // 2. Prefer parser-constrained decoding whenever the current prefix is not
  //    complete, so the produced text remains parser-valid.
  // 3. Use a boosted constrained step that explicitly favors the delimiter
  //    tokens "<<" and ">>", increasing the chance that arithmetic steps are
  //    written inside the required markers.
  // 4. If the parser reports the prefix is complete, stop early rather than
  //    risking invalid continuation.
  // 5. Respect eosToken by checking it before appending.
  //
